.idea
**/src/main/frontend/generated
# Vaadin prod/dev bundle: regenerated by a -Pproduction build (or the dev server).
# Not committed — SB-Emulators ships no production artifact and CI runs dev-mode, so the
# ~1MB blob's only cost here would be version-bump churn. Rebuilt on demand.
**/src/main/bundles/
# Vaadin dev-mode output at an app module's root (sampler/, a testapp stage), written by the
# dev server on first run. Nothing in it is hand-maintained here, so none of it is tracked.
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json
tsconfig.json
types.d.ts
vite.config.ts
vite.generated.ts
out

.settings
# Eclipse's compiled output. The launchers :migration-tool ships in its distribution zip
# live in a `bin` of their own and are source, so they are re-included below — a negation
# on the *directory*, since a file negation cannot escape an excluded parent.
bin
!**/src/main/dist/bin/
.classpath
.project
*.iml
.DS_Store

.claude/settings.local.json
**/.claude/.cc-writes/

# Agent git worktrees. Each is a checkout of this very repo, so `git add -A` from the
# main tree stages it as an *embedded repository* — a nested-repo pointer nobody wants
# and that a clone cannot resolve. Ignored so a routine `add -A` cannot commit one.
/.claude/worktrees/

target

# Adopted-testapp runtime debris. The documented launches set the app's working
# directory to target/run/, which `target` above already covers; these two catch a
# hand-run from a module directory, where an app that writes relative paths would
# otherwise drop a database file into the tree.
inventoryApp.db.mv.db
/testapps/*/*/log/

# adopt-testapp scratch root: an in-flight third-party app adoption (clone, its own
# local-only git history, per-app .m2, container build trees). Never committed here —
# the vetted app lands under testapps/<name>/swing/ at the end of the procedure.
/temp/
.vscode

# Python bytecode from the ideas/ measurement scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.playwright-mcp
